{
  "page_id": "AC-10",
  "section_header": "AIR CONDITIONING SYSTEM — On-Vehicle Inspection",
  "title": "ON-VEHICLE INSPECTION",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "1. CHECK CONDENSER FINS FOR BLOCKAGE OR DAMAGE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the fins are clogged, clean them with pressurized water."
    },
    {
      "type": "caution",
      "text": "Be careful not to damage the fins."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 1,
      "description": "Belt tension measurement diagram showing gauge placement between Nippondenso and Borroughs components, with measurement setup on engine components",
      "labels": [
        "Nippondenso",
        "Borroughs",
        "EG0603 EG0604 EG0601"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 25,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 20
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. CHECK DRIVE BELT TENSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Using a belt tension gauge, check the drive belt tension."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Belt tension gauge:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Manufacturer",
        "Part Number"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Nippondenso",
          "BTG-20 (95506-00020) or"
        ],
        [
          "Borroughs",
          "No. BT-33-73F"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Drive belt tension:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Belt Type",
        "Tension"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "New belt",
          "160 ± 20 lb"
        ],
        [
          "Used belt",
          "105 ± 10 lb"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "notice",
      "text": "NOTE:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "\"New belt\" refers to a belt which has been used less than 5 minutes on a running engine.",
        "\"Used belt\" refers to a belt which has been used on a running engine for 5 minutes or more."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. START ENGINE"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "4. TURN ON A/C SWITCH"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Check that the A/C operates at each position of the blower switch."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "5. CHECK MAGNETIC CLUTCH OPERATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "6. CHECK THAT IDLE INCREASES"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "When the magnetic clutch engages, engine revolution should increase."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Standard idle up rpm: 900 — 1,000 rpm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "7. CHECK AMOUNT OF REFRIGERANT"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If you can see bubbles in the sight glass, additional refrigerant is needed. (See page AC-11)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "8. IF NO OR INSUFFICIENT COOLING, INSPECT FOR LEAKAGE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Using a gas leak tester, inspect each component of the refrigeration system. (See page AC-11)"
    }
  ]
}
